    |
    = note: `name` is a parameter of the `pub` function `run_it`: a caller the compiler cannot see chooses the value, so nothing here says what it holds.
    = note: No check makes a stranger's choice of program safe: a name is looked up on `PATH`, a path runs that file.
    = note: `raw-sinks = "warn"` lets this build through.
    = help: Name the program with a literal, or choose it with a `match` whose arms are literals: `let editor = match env::var("EDITOR") ?? "" { "vim" => "vim", "nano" => "nano", else => "vi", }`. If the program means to run a program from outside, `untrusted-program = true` under `[allow]` in the manifest builds it.
warning[NK1308]: `dir` reaches the start of an argument of `process::run`, which the program may read as an option, and it comes from outside the program.
