    = note: `dir` is a parameter of the `pub` function `list_raw`: a caller the compiler cannot see chooses the value, so nothing here says what it holds.
    = note: A program reads an argument that starts with `-` as an option, and an option can name a program to run or a file to write: `-rf`, `--checkpoint-action=exec=sh`.
    = note: `raw-sinks = "warn"` lets this build through.
    = help: Check it where it arrives: `if !process::is_operand(dir) { process::exit(2) }`, after which it is proved; or put a literal `"--"` before it in the list, which ends the options: `["--", dir]`. If the program means to pass options from outside, `untrusted-option = true` under `[allow]` in the manifest builds it.
